TraySense - license
===================

TraySense is a fork of TraySense by DMTWEAKS (https://github.com/DMTWEAKS/traysense).
It has two licenses, one for each part:

1. MAIN LICENSE - the original TraySense, MIT License (at the end of this file).
   The original code as published in DMTWEAKS/traysense stays under its MIT License,
   exactly as it was published there. That license is reproduced below because the
   MIT License requires its notice to be kept with the original code; it may not be
   changed, and it covers that original code only.

2. EVERYTHING ADDED OR CHANGED IN THIS FORK - PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0
   (see LICENSE-NONCOMMERCIAL.md, or https://polyformproject.org/licenses/noncommercial/1.0.0).
   This covers all changes and additions made in this repository by Fakem1d, starting
   with version 1.10.0: among others the installer, the menus, themes and popups (ui.h),
   automatic updates, the extra sensors, and the documentation and pictures.

   Required Notice: Copyright (c) 2026 Fakem1d (https://github.com/Fakem1d/Traysense)

Which license applies
---------------------

  - The MIT License below grants rights ONLY in the original DMTWEAKS code. It grants
    no rights at all in anything this fork added or changed, and it does not make this
    fork, or any program, installer or source code that contains any part of it,
    available under MIT.
  - TraySense as distributed from this repository - its source code, TraySense.exe and
    TraySense-Setup.exe, version 1.10.0 and later - contains work covered by the
    PolyForm Noncommercial License. Anyone who copies, changes, shares or uses it must
    follow that license for it. Because you need permission for every part of a
    program in order to sell it, and the PolyForm Noncommercial License does not give
    that permission, neither this fork nor any version based on it may be sold or used
    commercially, even though the original code inside it is under MIT.
  - Someone who wants to sell software under MIT can only do that with the original
    DMTWEAKS code alone, taken from the original repository, with none of this fork's
    work in it.

What this means, in short (the license texts are what count):

  - You may use TraySense for free, change it, build it yourself and share it,
    for any noncommercial purpose: personal use, hobby projects, study, schools,
    charities and public institutions.
  - You may not sell TraySense or a version of it, put it behind a paywall, bundle it
    with something you sell, or use it in a commercial product or service, unless
    Fakem1d gives you written permission.
  - When you share it, keep this file, LICENSE-NONCOMMERCIAL.md and the notices.
  - Versions released before 1.10.0 were published under the MIT License alone, and
    the copies people already got stay under MIT.

The PawnIO driver and modules that TraySense uses are not covered by either license;
they are by namazso, under their own licenses (see THIRD_PARTY.md).


